@startuml chat_unread_uml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
hide footbox

title Messaging a seller, and how unread counts work

actor Buyer
actor Seller
participant "Chat screens\n(UI)" as UI
participant ChatService
participant Conversations
participant ChatRepository
participant OfferRepository

== Buyer sends the first message ==
Buyer -> UI : Send (text)
UI -> ChatService : messageSeller(listingId, text)
ChatService -> ChatService : check text is 1-1,000 characters,\nand listing is another seller's, available or reserved
note right of ChatService
  Each call runs in one database
  transaction on the service worker.
end note
ChatService -> Conversations : findOrStart(listing, buyer)
Conversations -> ChatRepository : find the buyer's conversation
alt no conversation yet
  Conversations -> ChatRepository : insert new Conversation
end
ChatService -> Conversations : append(conversation, buyer, text)
Conversations -> ChatRepository : insert next Message
Conversations -> ChatRepository : mark read up to it for the buyer
ChatService --> UI : ConversationView

== Seller's sidebar counts unread items ==
UI -> ChatService : getUnreadCount() after any navigation
loop each of the seller's conversations
  ChatService -> ChatRepository : count the buyer's messages\nafter the seller's read position
  ChatService -> OfferRepository : find the buyer's offers on the listing
  ChatService -> ChatService : add new and withdrawn offers\nsince the seller last opened it
end
ChatService --> UI : total unread
UI --> Seller : Conversations (1)

== Seller opens the conversation ==
Seller -> UI : open the conversation
UI -> ChatService : openConversation(conversationId)
ChatService -> ChatRepository : mark read up to the latest message,\nand record when the seller opened it
ChatService --> UI : ConversationView (every message)
UI -> ChatService : getUnreadCount() after the page loads
ChatService --> UI : total unread (this conversation now adds 0)

note over ChatService, OfferRepository
  Offer news needs no event table. The buyer counts accepted and
  rejected offers, the seller counts new and withdrawn ones, each
  only if it happened after that person last opened the conversation.
end note
@enduml
